1
00:00:08,790 --> 00:00:10,610
This is a national emergency.

2
00:00:12,430 --> 00:00:13,230
Detonator's charged!

3
00:00:26,680 --> 00:00:27,860
We're in a race against the Nazis.

4
00:00:31,030 --> 00:00:35,770
I know what it means if the Nazis have a bomb.

5
00:00:39,530 --> 00:00:40,910
We have a 12 -month head start.

6
00:00:41,310 --> 00:00:41,810
18.

7
00:00:41,830 --> 00:00:43,150
How could you possibly know that?

8
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:45,720
We've got one hope.

9
00:00:47,350 --> 00:00:51,210
All America's industrial might and scientific innovation connected here.

10
00:00:52,670 --> 00:00:53,450
Secret laboratory.

11
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:57,070
Keep everyone there until it's dark.

12
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:01,320
Let's go recruit some scientists.

13
00:01:04,890 --> 00:01:06,410
Build a town, build it fast.

14
00:01:06,410 --> 00:01:08,930
We don't let scientists bring their families.

15
00:01:09,110 --> 00:01:10,070
We'll never get the best.

16
00:01:12,080 --> 00:01:15,880
Why would we go to the middle of nowhere for who knows

17
00:01:15,880 --> 00:01:16,580
how long?

18
00:01:19,190 --> 00:01:19,690
Why?

19
00:01:20,040 --> 00:01:20,540
Why?

20
00:01:21,090 --> 00:01:22,810
How about because this is the most important thing

21
00:01:22,810 --> 00:01:24,530
to ever happen in the history of the world?

22
00:01:27,240 --> 00:01:32,550
You're the great improviser, but this you can't do in your head.

23
00:01:34,100 --> 00:01:37,100
Are we saying there's a chance that when we push that button,

24
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:39,300
we destroy the world?

25
00:01:40,140 --> 00:01:41,120
Chances are near zero.

26
00:01:43,020 --> 00:01:43,680
Near zero.

27
00:01:44,180 --> 00:01:45,440
What do you want from theory alone?

28
00:01:45,440 --> 00:01:47,410
Zero would be nice.

29
00:01:47,430 --> 00:01:54,290
It's a matter of life and death.

30
00:01:56,040 --> 00:01:57,500
I can perform this miracle.

31
00:01:59,940 --> 00:02:00,960
World War II would be over.

32
00:02:01,690 --> 00:02:02,790
Our boys would come home.

33
00:02:05,570 --> 00:02:06,510
It's happening, isn't it?

34
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:14,380
The world will remember this day.

35
00:02:18,140 --> 00:02:18,640
Kill.

36
00:02:19,940 --> 00:02:22,040
We'll ensure a peace mankind has never seen.

37
00:02:27,020 --> 00:02:28,480
Until somebody builds a bigger bomb.

38
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:37,040
You are the man who gave them the power to destroy themselves

39
00:02:38,250 --> 00:02:39,750
and the world is not prepared.

40
00:02:52,610 --> 00:02:59,690
Truman needs to know what's next.

41
00:03:00,310 --> 00:03:00,930
What's next?

42
00:03:01,450 --> 00:03:01,950
One.
